{
  "title": "Catalog: an alternatives line takes a food from the tail of an unknown brand name",
  "description": "\"2 containers Stonyfield’s Petite-Creme Vive la Vanilla or yogurt of choice\" (pipeline fixtures) resolves to vanilla extract: the first alternative names no food, so first_alternative (ramekin-core/src/catalog/resolve.rs) tries its trailing words and finds \"vanilla\". \
The estimate says \"Amount unclear (assumed vanilla)\" and reports a vanilla extract / container weight gap that make catalog-fill-weights would ask the model about. \
No calories are charged today, since a container of vanilla extract has no weight, but one estimated weight would make this line wrong. \
A null alias on the first alternative (\"stonyfield’s petite-creme vive la vanilla\") or on the whole item does not stop it: the trailing-words loop only asks whether the tail resolves directly. \
Possible fix: when the first alternative is itself a curated ambiguous (null) name, return no food instead of trying its tail; check the effect with make ingredient-catalog-audit and a before/after diff of logs/ingredient-catalog-failures.json, since \"x or y\" resolution touches many lines. \
Server-side only (ramekin-core catalog), so no web or iOS change.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "catalog",
    "nutrition",
